            "children": [
              {
                "_key": "5a7a63a19b63",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": "The lake stretches 1,200 km (750 mi) from north to south, with an average width of 320 km (200 mi). Its gross coverage is 386,400 km2 (149,200 sq mi) and the surface is about 27 m (89 ft) below "
              },
              {
                "_key": "54b069613d58",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [
                  "096f82f98664"
                ],
                "text": "sea level"
              },
              {
                "_key": "132b38657c37",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": ". Its main freshwater "
              },
              {
                "_key": "58f7978c78d7",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [
                  "4e5ca225fd00"
                ],
                "text": "inflow"
              },
              {
                "_key": "41d0e36291c5",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": ", Europe's longest river, the "
              },
              {
                "_key": "e1c0f644832a",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [
                  "5964125ff866"
                ],
                "text": "Volga"
              },
              {
                "_key": "a08caa2ddbc7",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": ", enters at the shallow north end. Two deep basins form its central and southern zones. These lead to horizontal differences in temperature, salinity, and ecology. The "
              },
              {
                "_key": "074169527eb0",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [
                  "aacb28b00e68"
                ],
                "text": "seabed"
              },
              {
                "_key": "27a86747e92a",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " in the south reaches 1,023 m (3,356 ft) below sea level, which is the third-lowest natural non-oceanic "
              },
              {
                "_key": "c8b31fa05f03",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [
                  "07a40a516644"
                ],
                "text": "depression"
              },
              {
                "_key": "605755fed0b9",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " on Earth after "
              },
              {
                "_key": "b890dcb4420f",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [
                  "19b3d877668b"
                ],
                "text": "Baikal"
              },
              {
                "_key": "f212380c114b",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "_key": "5ab2105cc629",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [
                  "3fd5268a31b6"
                ],
                "text": "Tanganyika"
              },
              {
                "_key": "5422d7f4379d",
                "_type": "span",
                "marks": [],
                "text": " lakes."
              }
            ],
